{"message":"Thanks — I can help with that. Quick math: $450 on $96,000 for one month implies an annualized rate of about 5.63% (450 / 96,000 × 12 ≈ 5.63%). Whether that’s “low” depends on the actual APY on your Gold savings, how interest is calculated (average daily balance, compounding frequency), any tiered rates that apply, and if any fees or promotional terms affected the payment.

I can look up your Gold savings account and your other accounts to confirm the exact APY, how interest was calculated, and whether you qualify for a higher rate — but I’ll need to verify your identity before accessing your account details. To proceed, tell me which identifier you want me to use to find your record (email, full name, or user ID), and then provide any two of the following for verification: date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY), email, phone number, or address. After you provide those I’ll verify and then check your rates and recent interest postings (I’ll also log the verification).

If you’d rather not verify right now, I can instead explain how to check the APY and interest calculation steps in your app and offer general tips to find better rates. Which would you prefer?" }
